<!--
  Session FSM — unicast, minimal-viable shape.

  Lowering of `docs/session-fsm.md` §2.1 unicast states + §2.2
  transitions + §2.4 close paths + §2.5 timer names + §2.7 accept-side
  hardening guards into a single SCE statechart-kind SCXML.

  Engine-free realization (R311il):
    Every effect is a native `<sce:action name=>` host-trait call — the
    same engine-free shape as `network/reassembly_slot.scxml` and
    `session/scouting.scxml`. No `<script>` bodies, so the generated
    `SessionFsmUnicastPolicy<A>` carries no `IScriptEngine` and the module
    compiles `#![no_std]` (codegen'd in no-std mode by
    wz-session-core/build.rs behind `#[cfg(feature = "session-unicast")]`).
    The host supplies behaviour by implementing the generated
    `SessionFsmUnicastActions` trait (18 no-arg methods, one per distinct
    action name) in `wz-runtime-tokio/src/session_glue.rs`.

    No-argument `<sce:action>` is admissible in `<onentry>`/`<onexit>` as
    well as on a `<transition>` (SCE pin 33ed5c4c9): an entry/exit effect
    that needs no triggering-event payload lowers to a bare trait call.
    That is why the entry/exit effects below stay declared once on their
    state (1:1 with the prose spec) instead of being copied onto every
    incoming/outgoing transition.

  Scope of this file:
  - Unicast paths only — the multicast variant is a separate file
    (`session_fsm_multicast.scxml`, deferred).
  - Active-mode scouting lives in `sources/session/scouting.scxml` and
    composes into this FSM at the Init level (the discovered locator is
    what `outbound.start` carries upward).
  - Established sub-regions (RX / TX / KeepAlive) from §2.3 are elided to
    a leaf state; those parallel sub-regions land in a later round.
  - The stateless_accept variant from §2.7 is excluded (same file shape
    with a cookie-only AwaitingInitSyn -> SentInitAck transition).

  Timeout ownership (engine-free no_std, mirrors scouting.scxml /
  reassembly_slot.scxml "Timeout ownership"):
    Under no-std codegen the generated machine binds `type Hal = NoOpHal`
    (now_ticks_ms() == 0), so a W3C SCXML 6.2 `<send delay>` is emitted
    but DEAD — its scheduled event can never fire because the no_std
    clock never advances. So this FSM arms NO timer of its own: it owns
    the timeout TRANSITIONS only (`link.open_timeout`, `init_ack.timeout`,
    `open_ack.timeout`, `accepting.inactivity_timeout`, `closing.timeout`),
    and the host drive loop owns the CLOCK, raising each event when its
    deadline elapses. The deadline VALUES stay spec-sourced (§2.5:
    link.open 5s, init_ack 2s, open_ack 2s, accepting.inactivity 1s,
    closing 100ms), carried host-side; SSOT is preserved — value = spec,
    transition = statechart, clock = runtime.

    Deadline scoping (host sweep must preserve the R311fa/R311fb shape):
    - The per-phase handshake deadlines (init_ack / open_ack) are armed
      and handled within their arming child (SentInitSyn / GotInitAck). A
      stale deadline that elapses after the phase advanced has no handler
      in scope in the sibling and is discarded. The host sweep therefore
      arms each per-phase deadline keyed to the arming child and cancels
      it when that child is exited.
    - The accept deadline (`accepting.inactivity_timeout`) is a SINGLE
      whole-handshake bound armed once on accept entry and handled on the
      parent `Accepting`, so it is caught from whichever child is current
      when it fires. Exactly one is ever in flight, so the staleness
      hazard cannot arise. It targets `Closed`, NOT `Closing`: a timed-out
      accept drops silently with no Close frame (§2.7 anti-amplification).

  Accept-side admission guards (§2.7), dispatcher-enforced:
    The three caps — half-open capacity + per-source token bucket (on
    init_syn) and cookie validation (on open_syn) — depend on HOST state
    (the half-open table, the token bucket, the cookie HMAC), not on the
    triggering event's wire payload, so they are not native `cond=`
    expressions. As with reassembly's in-order/out-of-order split, the
    host dispatcher PRE-CLASSIFIES: it evaluates the caps and injects
    `init_syn.received` / `open_syn.received` only when admission passes;
    on denial it injects nothing (silent drop, no Close frame —
    anti-amplification per the §2.7 trust-class hardening matrix). The
    transitions below are therefore unconditional in the statechart; the
    admission decision is owned by the dispatcher and documented here.

  Close-reason split on the establishment rejects (R311y823):
    `framing.error` closes INVALID and `establishment.ext_rejected` closes
    GENERIC, because zenoh makes that distinction on the wire and a peer
    reads the byte. Its establishment FSM tags each failure with the reason
    to close on: the InitAck BODY's size parameters get
    `close::reason::INVALID` (`unicast/establishment/open.rs:288,304`) while
    EVERY extension handler's error — QoS, Shm, Auth, MultiLink,
    LowLatency, Compression, Patch — gets `close::reason::GENERIC`
    (`open.rs:321-364`, and `accept.rs:234-356` on the other side), and
    `link.close(reason)` puts it in a `Close` before dropping the link
    (`unicast/link.rs:103-114`). zenoh-pico does not arbitrate: it returns
    `_Z_ERR_GENERIC` and sends no Close at all
    (`unicast/transport.c:141-152`).

    The new event exists ONLY on `Opening` and `Accepting`, which is the
    whole of establishment. An ext reject cannot arise once Established, and
    a handler-less event there is discarded by the engine — so the scope is
    enforced by the statechart rather than by a dispatcher convention.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:schemaLocation="http://sce.dev/ext sce-forge.xsd"
       sce:kind="statechart"
       name="session_fsm_unicast"
       version="1.0"
       initial="Init">

  <sce:session-role kind="accept-side"/>

  <state id="Init">
    <transition event="outbound.start" target="LinkOpening"/>
    <transition event="inbound.start" target="Accepting"/>
  </state>

  <state id="LinkOpening">
    <onentry>
      <sce:action name="link_driver_open"/>
    </onentry>
    <transition event="link.opened" target="Opening"/>
    <transition event="link.open_timeout" target="Closing">
      <sce:action name="set_close_reason_generic"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="link.lost" target="Closed"/>
  </state>

  <!--
    Per-phase handshake deadlines (init_ack / open_ack) are handled in
    their arming child so a stale host-raised deadline arriving in a later
    sibling has no handler in scope and is discarded (R311fa). The host
    sweep arms each deadline on entry to the child and cancels it on exit.
  -->
  <state id="Opening" initial="SentInitSyn">
    <state id="SentInitSyn">
      <onentry>
        <sce:action name="send_init_syn"/>
      </onentry>
      <transition event="init_ack.received" target="GotInitAck"/>
      <transition event="init_ack.timeout" target="Closing">
        <sce:action name="set_close_reason_generic"/>
      </transition>
    </state>
    <state id="GotInitAck">
      <onentry>
        <sce:action name="send_open_syn"/>
      </onentry>
      <transition event="open_ack.received" target="Established"/>
      <transition event="open_ack.timeout" target="Closing">
        <sce:action name="set_close_reason_generic"/>
      </transition>
    </state>
    <transition event="framing.error" target="Closing">
      <sce:action name="set_close_reason_invalid"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="establishment.ext_rejected" target="Closing">
      <sce:action name="set_close_reason_generic"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="peer.close" target="Closed"/>
    <transition event="link.lost" target="Closed"/>
  </state>

  <!--
    Accept-side whole-handshake deadline (`accepting.inactivity_timeout`,
    1s per §2.5) is armed once by the host on accept entry and handled on
    this parent, so it is caught from whichever child is current; targets
    Closed (silent drop, §2.7 anti-amplification). The init_syn / open_syn
    transitions are admission-gated by the dispatcher (see the header
    "Accept-side admission guards"), not by a native cond.
  -->
  <state id="Accepting" initial="AwaitingInitSyn">
    <state id="AwaitingInitSyn">
      <transition event="init_syn.received" target="SentInitAck"/>
    </state>
    <state id="SentInitAck">
      <onentry>
        <sce:action name="send_init_ack_with_cookie"/>
      </onentry>
      <transition event="open_syn.received" target="SentOpenAck"/>
    </state>
    <state id="SentOpenAck">
      <onentry>
        <sce:action name="send_open_ack"/>
      </onentry>
      <transition target="Established"/>
    </state>
    <transition event="accepting.inactivity_timeout" target="Closed"/>
    <transition event="framing.error" target="Closing">
      <sce:action name="set_close_reason_invalid"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="establishment.ext_rejected" target="Closing">
      <sce:action name="set_close_reason_generic"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="peer.close" target="Closed"/>
    <transition event="link.lost" target="Closed"/>
  </state>

  <state id="Established">
    <onentry>
      <sce:action name="enable_rx_tx_regions"/>
      <sce:action name="record_established_at"/>
      <sce:action name="start_lease_monitor"/>
      <sce:action name="start_keepalive_worker"/>
    </onentry>
    <onexit>
      <sce:action name="stop_keepalive_worker"/>
      <sce:action name="stop_lease_monitor"/>
    </onexit>
    <transition event="session.close" target="Closing">
      <sce:action name="set_close_reason_generic"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="lease.expired" target="Closing">
      <sce:action name="set_close_reason_expired"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="framing.error" target="Closing">
      <sce:action name="set_close_reason_invalid"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="tx.congestion.exhaust" target="Closing">
      <sce:action name="set_close_reason_unresponsive"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="peer.close" target="Closed"/>
    <transition event="link.lost" target="Closed"/>
  </state>

  <state id="Closing">
    <onentry>
      <sce:action name="send_close_frame_with_reason"/>
    </onentry>
    <transition event="closing.timeout" target="Closed"/>
    <transition event="link.lost" target="Closed"/>
  </state>

  <final id="Closed">
    <onentry>
      <sce:action name="release_link"/>
      <sce:action name="free_pool_slots"/>
    </onentry>
  </final>

</scxml>
